lacked the machine-parseable `## Verification` fenced yaml block (it had only a
prose `## Verification hooks` section). The reviewer explicitly confirmed the
substantive design is correct ("The substantive design now matches the task";
PR-002 resolved; remaining Uncertain items non-blocking).

This is a mechanical formatting defect, not a design decision, so the operator
amended outcome.md directly instead of spending another planner round: a
`## Verification` section with a fenced yaml block containing
`bash .redteam/scripts/verify.sh` (the project verify_command — always
trusted; no allowlist change) was inserted above the existing
`## Verification hooks` prose. That satisfies PR-001 as the reviewer specified
("Add the required parseable block, e.g. one command for
`bash .redteam/scripts/verify.sh`").

The plan is approved as amended. Proceed to implement.

USER_DECISION: APPROVE
